  "designConclusion": "The observed catalog ShareLocks block seven selected later DDL statements, but do not exclude commit of a previously applied uncommitted function replacement. An RR census remains at 333 while execution yields 444 with 43 locks held; old snapshots independently survive later lock acquisition. A participating writer transaction advisory lock drains before fresh READ COMMITTED observation (555), blocks a new participating writer, and permits reacquisition after reader release. A nonparticipating writer bypasses it (fresh census followed by different SQL text returning 666). Publication/commit exclusion covering every relevant pending writer and fresh source observation remain separate obligations. Exact endpoint source equality hides the demonstrated 666->777->666 routine history and intermediate native call. An unrelated application-data change is absent from the source census. Neither endpoint equality nor a source-only cut establishes full execution-to-disclosure authority.",
